     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.8999996185303px;margin-bottom:16px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:1.45;padding:16px;border-radius:3px;word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(51,51,51);background-color:rgb(247,247,247)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:11.8999996185303px;border-radius:3px;word-break:normal;display:inline;max-width:initial;overflow:initial;line-height:inherit;word-wrap:normal;background:transparent\">fit &lt;- cfa.run(dataframe, cfa_structure)\r\nsummary(fit)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Arial,freesans,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:22.3999996185303px;margin-bottom:0px!important\">What I want to do, for example, is return specific values like the p-value.</p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>If you want the <i>p</i> value for the chi-squared statistic, you can get it from the vector returned by<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> fitMeasures(fit)</font></div><div><br></div><div>If you want the <i>p</i> values for the parameter estimates, you can get them from the &quot;pvalue&quot; column in the output of<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> parameterEstimates(fit)</font></div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
